title: Start
---
Villager: I am busy right now. Talk to the right worker if you need help.
===

title: Lumber
---
Lumber: You want passage on that boat? Then you need more than timber.
Lumber: The Sailor needs a Spyglass tuned for storm light. Without it, he will not risk the black water.
Lumber: I can trade you one, but I need 60 Wood, 25 Stick, 12 iron, and 4 flaming_ore to reinforce the lens frame.
-> Trade the materials for the Spyglass <<if has_items("Wood:60|Stick:25|iron:12|flaming_ore:4")>>
    <<trade_items "Wood:60|Stick:25|iron:12|flaming_ore:4" "Spyglass" 1>>
    Lumber: Good. Take the Spyglass. Do not crack it before the Sailor sees it.
-> Why does the fisherman need that?
    Lumber: The coast past the bay folds into fog. The Spyglass sees the hidden reef lights before the hull is already dead.
-> What will you give me?
    Lumber: The Spyglass. It is one of the two things the Sailor will demand before letting you aboard.
-> I will come back.
    Lumber: Come back with 60 Wood, 25 Stick, 12 iron, and 4 flaming_ore. Anything less is not end-of-the-world work.
===

title: Miner
---
Miner: The Sailor still needs an Anchor strong enough for the deep current.
Miner: I can forge one, but not from common metal.
Miner: Bring me 15 diamond, 10 radium, 6 plasma, and 10 gold. Then I can make something that holds.
-> Trade the ore for the Anchor <<if has_items("diamond:15|radium:10|plasma:6|gold:10")>>
    <<trade_items "diamond:15|radium:10|plasma:6|gold:10" "Anchor" 1>>
    Miner: Done. Take the Anchor. If the chain breaks after this, it means the sea wanted you personally.
-> Why those materials?
    Miner: Diamond takes the pressure, gold carries the rune lines, radium hardens the Anchor, and plasma wakes it up.
-> What will you give me?
    Miner: The Anchor. The Sailor will not leave shore without it.
-> I will come back.
    Miner: Bring 15 diamond, 10 radium, 6 plasma, and 10 gold. If you are not ready for that, you are not ready for the sea.
===

title: Sailor
---
Sailor: My boat is not a ferry. Past the bay, the sea eats weak ships.
Sailor: If the Lumber traded you the Spyglass, and the Miner forged the Anchor, then maybe you are worth taking.
Sailor: Bring me both: the Spyglass and the Anchor. Then I will let you aboard.
-> Hand over the Spyglass and Anchor <<if has_items("Spyglass:1|Anchor:1")>>
    <<trade_items "Spyglass:1|Anchor:1" "SailBoat" 1>>
    Sailor: That is what I needed. The boat is yours to use. Do not waste the crossing.
-> Why do you need both?
    Sailor: The Spyglass finds the safe line through the fog. The Anchor keeps the boat from being dragged into the dark water. Missing either one gets us killed.
-> I have work to do.
    Sailor: Then prove you are at the end of your journey. I sail only when both repairs are ready.
===
